{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
The [Am]Diamond is a [G]ship, my lads,
For the [Am]Davis Strait she's [E]bound,
And the [Am]quay it is all [G]garnished
With [E]bonnie lasses [Am]round.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
So it's [C]cheer up, my [G]lads,
Let your [Am]hearts never [E]fail,
For the [C]bonnie ship the [G]Diamond
Goes a-[E]fishing for the [Am]whale.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
A[Am]long the quay at [G]Peterhead
The [Am]lasses stand a[E]roon',
Wi' their [Am]shawls all pulled a[G]round them
And the [E]saut tears runnin' [Am]doon.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: A shortened song: two of its traditional verses.}
{x_end: Am}
